 "samples": {
  "4242": "Years 0–49:\n[1] Eira told the day back as a story worth remembering — Eira's oral saga (Storytelling) has been invented!\n[1] Torv began carving a sign into a flat stone when something new is made — no one told them to.\n[4] Eira the Firebringer starved to death.\n[8] From that day on, Ask was known as Ask the Spearmaker.\n[39] Rune sewed clothes from hides — winter has met its match.",
  "97013": "Years 0–49:\n[1] Eira told the day back as a story worth remembering — Eira's oral saga (Storytelling) has been invented!\n[33] Bjorn set upon Liv the Founder and seized goods — the gap was cheaper to close by force.\n[34] In Livholm, the people have begun to listen when Ask the Ironhand speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership.\n[38] Need drove the hand: Bjorn took what could be carried from Liv the Founder.\n[39] Ask the Ironhand died of old age at 55.",
  "20260718": "Years 0–49:\n[1] Embla told the day back as a story worth remembering — Embla's the telling (Storytelling) has been invented!\n[1] From that day on, Ask was known as Ask the Firebringer.\n[27] Hunger owned the hand: Bjorn wrenched food from Torv the Rememberer.\n[38] Embla the Spearmaker died of old age at 57.\n[45] In Ylvahaven, the people have begun to listen when Eira speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership."
 },
